# Try the people endpoints by hand, using VS Code's REST Client extension or Visual Studio.
#
# They need an access token for a Family.Admin. To get yours: sign in to the web app, open
# the browser's dev tools, go to Network, click the `me` request, and copy the value after
# "Bearer " in its Authorization header. Paste it below. It lasts about an hour. Don't
# commit it, and remember this repo is public: use fictional people here.

@api = http://localhost:5080
@token = paste-your-access-token-here

### Add a person
POST {{api}}/api/v1/admin/people
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sex": "Female",
  "names": [
    { "givenName": "Isla", "surname": "Campbell", "type": "Birth" },
    { "givenName": "Isla", "surname": "MacLeod", "type": "Married" }
  ]
}

### List people, a page at a time
GET {{api}}/api/v1/admin/people?skip=0&take=50
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Read one person: replace the ID with one from the list
GET {{api}}/api/v1/admin/people/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Refused: a person needs a given name
POST {{api}}/api/v1/admin/people
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "names": [{ "surname": "MacLeod" }] }
